  <section>
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num" style="font-style: normal;">&sect;</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Further reading.</div>
        <p class="section-dek">Threads to pull on while I test the hypotheses above. Held lightly — I haven't digested all of them yet.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: grid; gap: 18px; max-width: 640px;">

      <div style="padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 4px;">Dave Mangot &mdash; <em>Agentic Proficiency: The New Premium Private Equity SaaS Valuation</em> (Apr 2026)</div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;">The clearest current framing of why harness engineering is a premium bet, not a feature. Mangot names four pillars underneath it &mdash; quality internal platforms, a healthy data ecosystem, AI-accessible internal data, and strong version control &mdash; and argues agentic proficiency is what now commands the private-equity SaaS multiple. Complementary to Finster's CD canon: Finster tells you how the pipeline has to behave; Mangot tells you why the market is starting to price it in.</p>
        <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;"><a href="https://blog.mangoteque.com/blog/2026/04/15/agentic-proficiency-the-new-premium-private-equity-saas-valuation/" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);">blog.mangoteque.com / agentic-proficiency</a></p>
      </div>

      <div style="padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 4px;">Bryan Finster &mdash; the continuous delivery canon, now re-applied to agents</div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;">Three decades of CI/CD experience, distilled into a minimum-viable definition &mdash; and, more recently, applied directly to agentic workflows. The clearest articulation I know of what "harness engineering" is actually rediscovering.</p>
        <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 4px;">
          <li style="font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.5;">&mdash; <a href="https://bryanfinster.com/blog/clarity-was-always-the-bottleneck" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);"><em>Clarity Was Always the Bottleneck</em></a> &mdash; on why AI didn't create the output-vs-outcome problem, it just made it impossible to hide.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.5;">&mdash; <a href="https://beyond.minimumcd.org/docs/agentic-cd/architecture/agentic-architecture/#how-skills-and-agents-relate" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);"><em>Agentic Architecture Patterns</em></a> &mdash; single responsibility, explicit interfaces, and separation of concerns applied to skills, agents, and commands.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.5;">&mdash; <a href="https://minimumcd.org" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);">minimumcd.org</a> and <a href="https://bryanfinster.com" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);">bryanfinster.com</a> &mdash; the underlying canon.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 4px;">DORA &mdash; <em>State of AI-assisted Software Development 2025</em></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;">Nearly 5,000 responses. Headline finding: AI amplifies the organisational system you already have &mdash; good or bad. Useful ammo for the outputs-vs-outcomes conversation.</p>
        <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;"><a href="https://dora.dev/research/2025/dora-report/" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);">dora.dev/research/2025/dora-report</a></p>
      </div>

      <div style="padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 4px;">McKinsey &mdash; <em>Unleashing developer productivity with generative AI</em></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;">The productivity-gains framing that's driving CTO expectations right now. Worth reading so I know what the ask from above actually looks like &mdash; and where the measurement gap opens up.</p>
        <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;"><a href="https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/tech-and-ai/our-insights/unleashing-developer-productivity-with-generative-ai" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);">mckinsey.com / unleashing-developer-productivity</a></p>
      </div>

      <div style="padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 4px;">Saed &mdash; <em>The State of B2B Product Management</em></div>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 6px;">425 responses across 37 countries, from a friend's survey. Flags strategy being sidelined by reactivity and discovery being under-prioritised &mdash; the same gap I keep hitting in sales calls.</p>
        <p style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;"><a href="https://b2bproduct.io/?flow" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);">b2bproduct.io</a></p>
